# Browser
# Drake Hatcher: "Whenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, put that many incubation counters on it." On turn 3
# it hits for 1 (one counter) and, with vigilance, stays untapped. On turn 5 casting Mox Jet (a noncreature spell) pumps it
# with prowess to 2/4 and it hits for 2, so the counters are 3: "that many" is the damage dealt, not the number of hits.
# "Remove three incubation counters": with one counter the ability is refused (a cost cannot be paid), with three it
# makes a 2/2 blue flying Drake token and the counters are gone. The refusal and its control are the same line.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Drake Hatcher
Mox Jet
Island
Island
Island
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Drake Hatcher.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 19
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters.Incubation = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Tapped = False
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters = 1 × incubation
! Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Activate(Ability: Create a 2/2)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Attack(Drake Hatcher)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 17
? Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Power = 2
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters = 3 × incubation
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Activate(Ability: Create a 2/2)

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Drake Token; Drake Hatcher; Island; Mox Jet; Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Hatcher.Counters.Incubation = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Token.Power = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Token.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Token.Colors = Blue
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Token.Subtypes = Drake
Bot1.Battlefield.Drake Token.Keywords = Flying
